      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Every interdiction counts. 80 percent of all narcotics seized are confiscated at sea, with drug smuggler continuing to seek ways to traffic illicit drugs into the U.S.  This diagram shows the inside of a narco-submarine used to move illegal drugs. By intercepting these vessels, the Coast Guard is protecting the American people from the threat of illegal drugs and disrupting criminal organizations.\n\nDrugs interdicted are lives saved. In 2025, the Coast Guard has seized over 49,000 pounds (22,000 kilograms) of illicit drugs per month. With lethal doses of narcotics being so miniscule, Coast Guard drug interdictions are saving countless lives. Our men and women are committed to keeping the American people safe by combatting drug trafficking and maximizing the Nation’s return on investment in the Coast Guard. @DHSgov #USCG #DrugInterdiction",
